{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "NEH",
  "chapter": 6,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "NEH.6.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.6.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now it came to pass, when Sanballat, and Tobiah, and Geshem the Arabian, and the rest of our enemies, heard that I had built the wall, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " there was no breach left in it, (though at that time I had not set up the doors upon the gates;)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.6.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.6.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That Sanballat and Geshem sent to me, saying, Come, let us meet together in ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "some one of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the villages in the plain of Ono. But they thought to do me mischief.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.6.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.6.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I sent messengers to them, saying, I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " doing a great work, so that I cannot come down: why should the work cease, whilst I leave it, and come down to you?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.6.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.6.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet they sent to me four times after this sort; and I answered them after the same manner.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.6.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.6.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Sanballat sent his servant to me in like manner the fifth time with an open letter in his hand;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.6.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.6.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " written, It is reported among the heathen, and Gashmu saith ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou and the Jews think to rebel: for which cause thou buildest the wall that thou mayest be their king, according to these words.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.6.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.6.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou hast also appointed prophets to preach of thee at Jerusalem, saying, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "There is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a king in Judah: and now shall it be reported to the king according to these words. Come now therefore, and let us take counsel together.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.6.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.6.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then I sent to him, saying, There are no such things done as thou sayest, but thou feignest them out of thy own heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.6.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.6.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For they all made us afraid, saying, Their hands shall be weakened from the work, that it may not be done. Now therefore, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "O God",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", strengthen my hands.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.6.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.6.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Afterward I came to the house of Shemaiah the son of Delaiah the son of Mehetabeel, who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shut up; and he said, Let us meet together in the house of God, within the temple, and let us shut the doors of the temple: for they will come to slay thee; yea, in the night will they come to slay thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.6.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.6.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I said, Should such a man as I flee? and who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", that, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "being",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", would go into the temple to save his life? I will not go in.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.6.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.6.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And lo, I perceived that God had not sent him; but that he pronounced this prophecy against me: for Tobiah and Sanballat had hired him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.6.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.6.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he hired, that I should be afraid, and do so, and sin, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they might have ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "matter",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for an evil report, that they might reproach me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.6.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.6.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My God, think thou upon Tobiah and Sanballat according to these their works, and on the prophetess Noadiah, and the rest of the prophets, that would have put me in fear.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.6.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.6.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So the wall was finished in the twenty and fifth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "day",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the month",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Elul, in fifty and two days.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.6.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.6.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass, that when all our enemies heard ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and all the heathen that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " about us saw ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "these things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", they were much cast down in their own eyes: for they perceived that this work was wrought by our God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.6.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.6.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Moreover, in those days the nobles of Judah sent many letters to Tobiah, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the letters",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of Tobiah came to them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.6.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.6.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " many in Judah sworn to him, because he ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the son-in-law of Shechaniah the son of Arah; and his son Johanan had taken the daughter of Meshullam the son of Berechiah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NEH.6.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:NEH.6.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Also they reported his good deeds before me, and uttered my words to him. ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "And",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Tobiah sent letters to put me in fear.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
